From c74016da7b93889d2f00adaff44ba78842c1dca6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:11:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] camera: camera_settings.conf holds the mode ladder

Why: The port kept the mode ladder in a second settings file,
mode_ladder.conf, with its own path function, its own atomicWrite call
under the command lock, its own read-back check and a file text with a
ticket number in its header (CameraController.cpp:404-430 and
11858-11892@cinemate-port). Original Apertar has one place for camera-wide
settings: camera_settings.conf, written by Core only through the debounced
persister, one key per setting, carried across the format profiles like
tuning_file (CameraController.cpp:7939-7955 and :742-889@upstream-1.6.0).
A second file means a second writer and a second failure path.

What: CaptureSettings holds the ladder as four persisted fields:
modeLadderEnabled, modeLadderRampReady, modeLadderResolutions and
modeLadderAspects (the aspect filter was added to the port after the plan
was written, so it needs its key too). The loader reads mode_ladder_enabled,
mode_ladder_ramp_ready, mode_ladder_resolutions and mode_ladder_aspects in
every block, the writer writes them in every block, and the format switch
carries them over. modeLadder_ stays the parsed form; the constructor
builds it from the settings with the new ladder::fromText, and
setModeLadder sets it together with the fields. A ladder edit saves
through persistSettingsLocked, a rung or format change through
applySettingsLocked, as the tuning file does, and the filter alone
persists with no apply and no settings event, as before. While none of the
four keys is in camera_settings.conf, an existing mode_ladder.conf is read
once at start and taken over (also when camera_settings.conf is missing);
the old file is never written or deleted. A preset keeps the camera's
ladder. Deleted: saveModeLadderLocked, saveModeLadderAspectsLocked,
ladder::fileText, ladder::withAspectsLine and the "could not write
mode_ladder.conf" warning, which the persister's own log line replaces.
parseFile now builds on fromText. The active ladder still blocks
set_resolution, set_raw_bit_depth and set_clear_hdr and ladderOverride_
stays unsaved.

Tested: check_core.sh both builds and the host tests pass with no new
warning (mode_ladder_test covers fromText and the take-over parse). In
--simulate with a fresh HOME: a mode_ladder.conf is taken over at the first
start, the first settings change writes the four keys with the same
resolutions text, and a restart without the old file shows the same ladder;
set_mode_ladder (resolutions, enabled, aspects) persists across a restart;
a record format switch cdng, h264, cdng keeps the ladder; set_mode_ladder
enabled=false is accepted in Standby; set_resolution is still refused while
the ladder is on. The smoke shapes match 1.6.0's. Needs the camera: the
ladder on the owner's rig is unchanged after the update. Run
get_mode_ladder before and after and diff the two replies, then one
set_resolution with the ladder on (expect the refusal, not a ladder
switch-off).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
